<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH FUND BOHATSTVI POSTS 9MO LOSS.</title>
<headline>CZECH FUND BOHATSTVI POSTS 9MO LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for nine</p>
<p>months ending September 30, 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross result	 407.131 loss   vs	 61.566 profit</p>
<p> Operating loss	 2.531	  vs	  1.323</p>
<p> Total revenue    3,647.907	  vs	    n/a</p>
<p> Total costs	4,055.038	  vs	    n/a</p>
<p> Total assets     3,544.804	  vs    2,467.678</p>
<p> Basic capital    1,255.527	  vs    1,255.527</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Bohatstvi IF</p>
<p>a.s. . It is an investment fund managed by 1.</p>
<p>Investicni a.s., the investment arm of bank IPB a.s. .</p>
<p>According to the latest available information, IPB held</p>
<p>25.3 percent of the fund's shares at the end of the last month.</p>
<p>The results were provided by the fund managers.</p>
<p>Bohatstvi shares are listed on the main market of the</p>
<p>Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
